# The unit suite is the assertion, constraint, comparator, mock-object and metadata code
# that every other project's verdict passes through.
#
# The other suite this project ships, `end-to-end`, is NOT here yet, and the reason is a
# measurement rather than a preference: one of its 805 cases -- a test whose data
# provider yields an array that contains itself -- does not terminate under this engine.
# A self-referential array that leaves the function that built it comes back with its
# cycle flattened into an unbounded nesting, so the exporter that prints the data set
# descends for ever. A step that has to be killed on a timer answers a different question
# on every run, which is the one thing a baseline cannot be. It goes in when that
# terminates.
unit	$PHL_VENDOR_ENGINE phpunit --testsuite unit --no-coverage
